  "_comment": "Log redaction vectors for platform-gincommon internal/core/service/log_sanitizer.go (isSensitiveLogKey, Sanitize, SanitizeString), fastapicommon logging/sanitize.py and @platform/frontend-sdk/core (isSensitiveKey, sanitizeFields, sanitizeString). `keys`: whether a field name is sensitive. `fields`: a flat field map before and after redaction (every value of a sensitive key becomes [REDACTED], whatever its type; the TypeScript SDK also recurses into nested objects, which the flat backends never receive, and tests that separately). `strings`: SanitizeString removes Unicode Cc characters, then truncates to 256 UTF-8 bytes at a character boundary. `expectedSdk`, when present, is the TypeScript SDK's result where it is deliberately stricter: it also removes U+2028 and U+2029 (design doc /core). Go cannot run this file until gincommon exports its sanitizer (design doc D6 I).",
